---
import PostLayout from '../../layouts/PostLayout.astro';
import { posts } from '../../data/posts';
const post = posts.find((p) => p.slug === 'retention-playbook');
const title = 'How to Reduce Patient Attrition: The Dental Loyalty Playbook, Retain Dental'
const description = 'A practical 5-step framework to cut patient attrition in your dental practice, built from the data of 12 pilot clinics on Retain Dental.'
const pageUrl = 'https://retaindental.com/blog/retention-playbook'
const publishedDate = '2026-06-10'
const modifiedDate = '2026-06-16'
---

<PostLayout
  title={title}
  description={description}
  canonical={pageUrl}
  slug={post?.slug ?? 'retention-playbook'}
  author={post?.author}
  date={post?.date ?? publishedDate}
  tags={post?.tags ?? []}
  quickAnswer={post?.quickAnswer}
>


      <div class="prose prose-lg max-w-none text-text-600 space-y-6">
        <p class="text-xl text-text-600 leading-relaxed font-medium">
          Most dental practices lose 15-20% of their active patients every year. Not because the
          clinical care is bad, because nobody has built a system to keep patients engaged
          between visits.
        </p>

        <h2 class="text-3xl font-semibold text-text-900 mt-12 mb-4 tracking-tight">The math on attrition</h2>
        <p>
          The average dental practice has 1,800 active patients. Industry data says 18% will churn
          annually. That's 324 patients walking out the door every year, patients you already
          paid to acquire.
        </p>
        <p>
If the average patient lifetime value is $450, you're losing <strong>$175,000</strong> in
           foregone revenue every year. Per practice. Per year.
        </p>

        <h2 class="text-3xl font-semibold text-text-900 mt-12 mb-4 tracking-tight">The 5-step retention playbook</h2>

        <h3 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-text-900 mt-8 mb-3">1. Stop renting your audience</h3>
        <p>
          If your only relationship with patients is Instagram, you don't have a practice, you have
          an ad dependency. Move them to a channel you own: a branded patient app.
        </p>

        <h3 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-text-900 mt-8 mb-3">2. Reward the behavior you want</h3>
        <p>
          Tiers work. Patients who reach Gold status attend 2.4x more appointments per year than
          Member patients. Household points, where family members pool balances, drives 3.2x
          higher multi-patient enrollments.
        </p>

        <h3 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-text-900 mt-8 mb-3">3. Make re-care automatic, not aspirational</h3>
        <p>
          The practices that retain patients treat re-care as a system, not a task. Automated
          reminders at 5.5 months, 6 months, and 6.5 months catch the patient before they forget.
        </p>

        <h3 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-text-900 mt-8 mb-3">4. Track compliance, not just appointments</h3>
        <p>
          A patient who shows up but doesn't wear their aligners is a future no-show. Live
          protocol monitoring, daily check-ins for Invisalign, post-op, etc., keeps the clinical
          outcome (and the relationship) on track.
        </p>

        <h3 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-text-900 mt-8 mb-3">5. Treat referrals as a feature</h3>
        <p>
          Your happiest patients are your cheapest acquisition channel. Build the referral mechanic
          into the loyalty tier, not as a separate "ask for a referral" email.
        </p>

        <h2 class="text-3xl font-semibold text-text-900 mt-12 mb-4 tracking-tight">What the pilot data shows</h2>
        <p>
          Across 12 pilot clinics running Retain Dental for 90+ days, we measured:
        </p>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2 text-text-600">
          <li><strong>41% reduction</strong> in recall no-shows</li>
          <li><strong>3.2x</strong> household enrollments vs solo-clinic app</li>
          <li><strong>2.4x</strong> appointment frequency for Gold-tier patients</li>
          <li><strong>14 days</strong> average time to first app install after launch</li>
        </ul>

        <div class="mt-12 p-6 bg-ink-900 rounded-2xl text-white">
          <h3 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-2">Try Retain Dental free for 14 days</h3>
          <p class="text-text-onDark-500 text-sm mb-4">Live on your real patients in 20 minutes.</p>
          <a href="https://app.retaindental.com" class="inline-block px-6 py-3 bg-white text-ink-900 rounded-full font-semibold transition-transform">
            Start free trial →
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</PostLayout>
